# 4. Meeting the Printer That Isn't a Printer

To confirm it was actually speaking LPD, I sent a raw queue status command by hand.

```bash
printf '\x04archive_intake\n' | nc -q2 paperwork.htb 1515
```

```text
Archive_Printer is ready and printing.
```

> **📝 My Explanation:**

There it was. A live, custom LPD implementation, replying like an overly enthusiastic office printer that has never actually printed anything in its life. Real `lpd` does not typically greet you with a cheerful status line like that, which was clue number one that this was a homegrown Python service cosplaying as a real printer daemon.

I scripted a full RFC 1179 job submission in Python, because raw netcat does not handle the binary framing and ACK bytes gracefully, and confirmed the handshake worked end to end. Every step came back with a clean `\x00` ACK, meaning the daemon happily swallowed a completely harmless test job.

### Working RFC 1179 client (benign test)

```python
import socket

target = "10.129.248.117"
port = 1515
queue = "archive_intake"

def send_recv(s, data):
    s.sendall(data)
    return s.recv(4096)

s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
s.connect((target, port))

resp = send_recv(s, f"\x02{queue}\n".encode())
print("Job init:", resp)

job_id = "001"
hostname = "kali"
cfile_name = f"cfA{job_id}{hostname}"
cfile_content = f"Hhostname\nPuser\nJtestjob\nldfA{job_id}{hostname}\n"

resp = send_recv(s, f"\x02{len(cfile_content)} {cfile_name}\n".encode())
print("CF header ack:", resp)
resp = send_recv(s, cfile_content.encode() + b"\x00")
print("CF content ack:", resp)

dfile_name = f"dfA{job_id}{hostname}"
dfile_content = "hello from paperwork lab test\n"

resp = send_recv(s, f"\x03{len(dfile_content)} {dfile_name}\n".encode())
print("DF header ack:", resp)
resp = send_recv(s, dfile_content.encode() + b"\x00")
print("DF content ack:", resp)

s.close()
```

```text
Job init: b'\x00'
CF header ack: b'\x00'
CF content ack: b'\x00'
DF header ack: b'\x00'
DF content ack: b'\x00'
```

Five clean ACKs. The printer accepted the job like it had nothing better to do, which, to be fair, it did not.

